Everyone chill. yeah?

227
00:10:05.083 --> 00:10:07.041
Ugh! Why did you piss everywhere?

228
00:10:07.125 --> 00:10:08.625
- Defense.
- What are you. a skunk?

229
00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.958
- He fucking smells like one.
- No. I'm a cat.

230
00:10:11.041 --> 00:10:13.875
And I piss where I like.
Shows territory. ownership.

231
00:10:13.958 --> 00:10:15.916
- So technically. it's mine now.
- What is?

232
00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:18.541
- [cats yelp]
- Fucking hell!

233
00:10:18.625 --> 00:10:22.208
Jesus Christ. Everyone calm the fuck down.

234
00:10:22.291 --> 00:10:24.208
[sighs] Let's go.

235
00:10:24.291 --> 00:10:26.041
[soft guitar music playing]

236
00:10:30.291 --> 00:10:31.625
Huh. Do you mind?

237
00:10:31.708 --> 00:10:32.666
Go for it.

238
00:10:35.416 --> 00:10:37.208
- Good work.
- Yeah. nice one.

239
00:10:37.291 --> 00:10:38.875
Shoo! Shoo! Get out of here!

240
00:10:38.958 --> 00:10:39.958
- Fuck off!
- Yeah!

241
00:10:40.041 --> 00:10:41.291
- Get fucked.
- Twat.

242
00:10:41.375 --> 00:10:43.666
{\an8}[soft music continues]

243
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.000
{\an8}- Why did you knock that plant over?
- He's a cat.

244
00:10:46.083 --> 00:10:48.125
{\an8}- So?
- So he's a bit of an arsehole.

245
00:10:48.208 --> 00:10:51.875
{\an8}- Am I a bit of an arsehole?
- Uh. not yet. but you've got potential.

246
00:10:51.958 --> 00:10:53.333
{\an8}Yeah. stick with us.

247
00:10:54.833 --> 00:10:55.833
I'm hungry.

248
00:10:55.916 --> 00:10:57.833
We all are. Get used to it.

249
00:10:57.916 --> 00:10:59.500
Well. actually. I'm not.

250
00:10:59.583 --> 00:11:01.333
No. you said. You've eaten.

251
00:11:01.416 --> 00:11:02.416
I have. yeah.

252
00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.625
Actually. in nine minutes.
my little timer opens up

253
00:11:05.708 --> 00:11:07.750
and I get some dried food and some milk.

254
00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:09.541
Why's your food on a timer?

255
00:11:09.625 --> 00:11:12.125
Well. the family are away for the evening.
They leave my food.

256
00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:14.583
and I pop in the cat flap.
wait for it to open.

257
00:11:14.666 --> 00:11:16.666
and then snooze
in a big. lovely empty house.

258
00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.250
Whoa. whoa.
your house is empty at the moment?

259
00:11:19.333 --> 00:11:21.541
- With loads of cat food?
- And there's a cat flap?

260
00:11:21.625 --> 00:11:23.291
Yeah. why?

261
00:11:23.375 --> 00:11:24.750
[gobbling hungrily]

262
00:11:24.833 --> 00:11:27.958
Oh. leave some of the salmon.
I mean. you're meant to digest it slowly.

263
00:11:28.041 --> 00:11:29.458
- [cats belching]
- Okay.

264
00:11:29.541 --> 00:11:30.916
- See you tomorrow.
- Gross.

265
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.583
- Twat.
- Thanks very much. guys.

266
00:11:32.666 --> 00:11:34.625
- Now I'm gonna be hungry. Bye.
- Bye.

267
00:11:34.708 --> 00:11:37.833
- Night-night. cunt.
- Right. Careful on the flap!

268
00:11:40.041 --> 00:11:42.041
[pensive music playing]

269
00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:47.583
Hey. That's my mate. Ralfy!

270
00:11:48.166 --> 00:11:49.250
- Gus!
- [Gus] Hey!

271
00:11:49.333 --> 00:11:51.208
- [Gus gasps] Ralfy!
- No!

272
00:11:51.958 --> 00:11:53.125
[Gus gasps sadly]

273
00:11:53.916 --> 00:11:55.583
Driver didn't even stop.

274
00:11:56.083 --> 00:11:57.250
No.

275
00:11:57.333 --> 00:11:59.958
They don't have to.
After all. it's just a cat.

276
00:12:00.666 --> 00:12:02.291
People don't care about us.

277
00:12:02.833 --> 00:12:05.291
People don't care
about anything except themselves.

278
00:12:05.791 --> 00:12:08.125
They don't even care about each other.
to be honest.

279
00:12:09.666 --> 00:12:10.750
It's sad.

280
00:12:11.291 --> 00:12:13.041
It happens. kid. [sighs sadly]

281
00:12:13.125 --> 00:12:16.750
I guess we're all future roadkill.
aren't we?

282
00:12:16.833 --> 00:12:20.041
Better than slowly dying
in a hovel of starvation.

283
00:12:20.541 --> 00:12:22.250
Or in agony from kidney failure.

284
00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.541
Is that how I'll die?

285
00:12:25.041 --> 00:12:26.083
[Gus] No.

286
00:12:26.958 --> 00:12:29.583
We'll find your home.
and you'll be taken to a vet

287
00:12:29.666 --> 00:12:33.500
when you're old and you'll be given
a lovely lethal injection.

288
00:12:33.583 --> 00:12:34.875
- Nice.
- [Gus] Mm.

289
00:12:34.958 --> 00:12:36.958
You won't die for ages though.

290
00:12:37.041 --> 00:12:38.958
What does being dead feel like?

291
00:12:39.541 --> 00:12:41.416
{\an8}It feels like nothing.

292
00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.666
{\an8}It… it feels like you did
before you were born.

293
00:12:45.166 --> 00:12:50.000
{\an8}You don't even know you're dead.
It's just everyone else does.

294
00:12:50.083 --> 00:12:52.166
{\an8}So you'll just never see him again?

295
00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.208
Exactly.

296
00:12:54.083 --> 00:12:55.916
We'll just never see him again.

297
00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.458
Well. we'll probably see him again
tomorrow. actually.

298
00:12:58.958 --> 00:13:01.208
'Cause the bin men
don't come till Thursday.

299
00:13:01.791 --> 00:13:03.916
[grunts] Unless a fox gets him tonight.

300
00:13:05.458 --> 00:13:07.791
["Hammer and Felt"
by Beneath The Mountain playing]

301
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.875
[music continues]

302
00:13:39.291 --> 00:13:41.791
Sorry we didn't find your house.
We'll find it tomorrow.

303
00:13:41.875 --> 00:13:45.583
- What if we don't find it tomorrow?
- Well. we'll find it the next day. then.

304
00:13:45.666 --> 00:13:47.458
What if we don't find it the next day?

305
00:13:47.541 --> 00:13:49.541
[groans wearily] We'll give up.

306
00:13:50.041 --> 00:13:51.083
[Kitten sighs sadly]

307
00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.666
I'm joking.

308
00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:58.541
We'll keep looking until we do find it.
all right? Just cheer up.

309
00:14:07.666 --> 00:14:09.708
[music fades]

310
00:14:09.791 --> 00:14:10.958
[Gus yawns]

311
00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.750
Home sweet home.

312
00:14:13.833 --> 00:14:16.000
- Good night.
- Night. mate.

313
00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.625
{\an8}Right. you sleep there. All right?

314
00:14:18.708 --> 00:14:21.750
It's not the Ritz.
but it'll keep you alive.

315
00:14:21.833 --> 00:14:22.916
Thank you.

316
00:14:25.041 --> 00:14:27.041
- [wind rustling]
- [dog barking]

317
00:14:35.041 --> 00:14:36.708
It's dark.

318
00:14:36.791 --> 00:14:39.916
Yeah. you're a cat.
You can see in the dark.

319
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.666
Yeah. but I don't like what I see.

320
00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:44.458
This is a scary place.

321
00:14:44.541 --> 00:14:49.541
Yeah. life's cruel. but you gotta stand
on your own four feet. yeah?

322
00:14:50.041 --> 00:14:52.333
No one can help you but you. kid.

323
00:14:54.125 --> 00:14:55.333
[sadly] Okay.

324
00:14:58.291 --> 00:15:00.000
[Kitten whimpers]

325
00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.583
[Kitten mewls. cries softly]

326
00:15:04.708 --> 00:15:06.708
- [Gus sighs]
- [Kitten cries]

327
00:15:07.833 --> 00:15:09.958
[poignant music playing]

328
00:15:10.041 --> 00:15:12.041
[Kitten whimpers]

329
00:15:17.291 --> 00:15:18.791
Thanks. Gus.

330
00:15:29.125 --> 00:15:31.333
[music fades]

331
00:15:33.916 --> 00:15:36.458
[rain pattering]

332
00:15:37.305 --> 00:16:37.905
